1
00:00:00,463 --> 00:00:01,673
(Bernadette:)I was thinking of going
to the lecture

2
00:00:01,831 --> 00:00:03,671
(Bernadette:)on posterior cingulate
cortex lesions

3
00:00:03,833 --> 00:00:05,713
(Bernadette:)in the formation
of autobiographical memory.

4
00:00:05,868 --> 00:00:07,848
(Amy:)Oh, brain lesions are fascinating.

5
00:00:08,004 --> 00:00:10,814
(Amy:)Unless they're yours,
than they're a drag.

6
00:00:12,175 --> 00:00:13,345
(Bernadette:)To the advancement of science.

7
00:00:13,509 --> 00:00:16,319
(Amy:)And to the sick and dying
who make it possible.

8
00:00:18,648 --> 00:00:21,688
(Bernadette:)This is fun. We never really get
to talk shop with Penny around.

9
00:00:21,851 --> 00:00:23,451
(Bernadette:)We usually just end up
talking about boys.

10
00:00:23,619 --> 00:00:25,899
(Amy:)Which is fine,
but it's nice to mix it up

11
00:00:26,055 --> 00:00:27,655
(Amy:)with a little
intellectual conversation.

12
00:00:27,824 --> 00:00:30,304
(Waiter:)From the two gentlemen at the bar.

13
00:00:30,460 --> 00:00:33,300
Oh, my gosh, boys bought us drinks!
Boys bought us drinks!

14
00:00:34,731 --> 00:00:36,331
(Amy:)Thank you, thank you,
thank you so much.

15
00:00:37,900 --> 00:00:40,140
(Bernadette:)-Be cool.
-You be cool!

16
00:00:40,303 --> 00:00:43,513
(Amy:)Guys are hitting on us,
and not just to get to Penny.

17
00:00:44,240 --> 00:00:47,310
You're right. Thank you!

18
00:00:51,814 --> 00:00:55,764
-Oh! Bad move.
-Really? Why?

